    "submission": "submission.json",
    "summary": "Submitted a research product that closes the configuration behavior's last open question with the executed restart result.\n\nContext from the index: the restart check was reviewed and accepted as a bounded negative (conclusion oblig-restart-config-log-backed: bounded_no_violation), so the run now holds three confirmed in-scope violations plus one bounded negative; unit admission is exhausted, with 4 experiments, 2 semantic reviews and 4 revisions still available.\n\nProduct contents (draft-relative submission.json with the updated map.json):\n\nMap clarification for b-config-change, citing SR-CONFIG-ENTRY, SR-NEWRAFT, SR-APPEND-CONFIG and SR-LEADER-LOOP. It adds the sourced recovery branch — the configuration is not stored apart from the log, NewRaft rebuilds it by scanning configuration entries through processConfigurationLogEntry, and the executed restart observed the node re-deriving the log-encoded single-voter configuration rather than the committed unpersisted one — together with the protection that recovery reads configuration state only from stored entries, so the in-memory adoption is confined to the running instance. The answered restart question is replaced by the one independent residual: whether an application FSM that applied entries under the lost configuration is consistent with the configuration re-derived after a restart.\n\nThe accompanying feedback (ref_ids b-config-change) records the measured answer, including that the implication held vacuously because the restarted node reported the log-encoded configuration, and refreshes the whole remaining frontier: the FSM-consistency question, the election-restriction chain, the heartbeat term-regression pair and the shutdown non-response, the pre-vote and TimeoutNow liveness residuals, and the out-of-snapshot readout/majority-intersection questions. Unit admission exhaustion is stated so the residuals are retained rather than converted into new obligations.\n\nPreflight `validate` returned valid=true with no diagnostics. Acceptance and the final map version remain with the controller."
